zune-capi: decode PNG headers before asking the decoder for the depth

`PngDecoder::depth()` returns `None` until the headers have been parsed, and
the PNG arm of `imdecode_inner` calls it straight after `PngDecoder::new`, so
the `unwrap()` always panics and the unwind out of an `extern "C"` function
aborts every C-side PNG decode.  `decode_headers()` returns
`Result<(), PngDecodeErrors>`, which the existing `From` impl lets `?` convert,
and it is idempotent, so the call `decode_into` makes internally is a no-op.
The PPM and PSD arms already decode headers first; the arms that only call
`decode_into` let the decoder do it.

--- a/crates/zune-capi/src/imread.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-capi/src/imread.rs
@@ -380,6 +380,7 @@
                 // we expect the caller to have appropriately taken care of allocating enough to hold 16 bit
                 //
                 let mut decoder = PngDecoder::new(data);
+                decoder.decode_headers()?;
 
                 match decoder.depth().unwrap() {
                     BitDepth::Eight => {
